From 5097ef8609ab960cd63f451130f85afcc05d812c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colorburst <dev@colorburst.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:25:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ChromeOS: a device-local account, and an OOBE entry point
 for it

Adds AccountType::LOCAL -- an account that exists only on this device,
with no gaia id, no OAuth tokens and nothing on a server -- and a new
OOBE screen that creates one, reachable from a third card on
UserCreationScreen ("Without a Google Account").

Design notes:

* No new user_manager::UserType. A local account is an ordinary
  kRegular user; what makes it local is its AccountId. Adding a UserType
  value would have meant touching 26 non-test exhaustive switches, a
  static_assert on kMaxValue, the policy proto and enums.xml. Instead
  User::HasGaiaAccount() now asks whether the AccountId really is a
  Google account, which is what its ~45 call sites actually mean and
  fixes them all at once -- including the CHECK(!gaia_id.empty()) in
  UserSessionManager::InitProfilePreferences that a non-Gaia AccountId
  used to die on.

* AccountType::LOCAL rather than reusing UNKNOWN, because UNKNOWN does
  not round-trip: user_manager::StoreAccountId never writes it, and
  LoadAccountId reads a missing account_type back as GOOGLE. A local
  account would come back after a reboot as a Gaia user with an empty
  gaia id.

* The screen collects a name, not a password. CompleteLogin() with no
  key takes AuthSessionAuthenticator's "new persistent user" path, which
  creates and mounts the cryptohome without a knowledge factor on
  purpose; upstream's PasswordSelectionScreen then sees no online
  password, forces LOCAL_PASSWORD_FORCED, and LocalPasswordSetupScreen
  writes the password.local-password auth factor. No cryptohome code and
  no password code is added here, and auth_session_authenticator.cc is
  untouched.

Two upstream inconsistencies fixed along the way:

* UserManagerImpl::SaveUserType() keyed prefs::kUserType by
  GetAccountIdKey() unconditionally, which is NOTREACHED() (fatal, also
  in official builds) for a non-Google AccountId. The reader of the same
  pref already falls back to the e-mail; the writer now matches it.

* The two places that rebuild the LoggedInUsers pref from
  persisted_users_ filtered on HasGaiaAccount(), which would silently
  drop a local user from the login screen's pod list. They now filter on
  the user type, which is what list membership actually means.

Finally, when --disable-gaia-services is set the setup-type screen hides
the "You" and "A child" cards, since both lead to a Gaia webview that
cannot load, and preselects the local card instead.
